---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}`}
  description={courseMeta.title}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A lecture theatre reduced to flat gold and black shapes, rows of seats sweeping past the frame, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <p>
    CCS-based augmentations -- cybernetic organisms that alter your brain’s activity and chemistry -- are a powerful new tool allowing you to think faster and smarter. Moving beyond its obvious uses in solving difficult problems in academia, this course will teach you the skills you need to harness your new second inner monologue in the most optimal way possible. Although this is a skill transferrable to any domain, we will do so chiefly for the creation of art: visual, literary, and auditory. In the weekly lectures you’ll learn fundamental concepts and practical skills for harnessing your cybernetic organ including how best to communicate with them. Then in the weekly workshops, you’ll give a brief presentation on the art that you’ve created and receive constructive criticism from your peers and tutor. However, the goal is to evaluate your interactions with the CCS rather than the artwork itself -- so no prior art experience is required. Hence, by the end of the course you’ll have created multiple artworks, but you’ll have gained a significantly better understanding of using your organ toward any mean.
  </p>

  <h2>Quick Links</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each {sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
